(9,27,'“He might keep his shape long enough to postpone the wedding,” said Sir James.','Restore the mould metaphor.'),
(12,43,'“What would you think of me if I came down two hours after everyone else and ordered a grilled bone?”','Restore the comparison Rosamond makes between her conduct and Fred’s.'),
(16,19,'Laure paused again, then said slowly, “_I meant to do it._”','Restore emphasis on deliberate action.'),
(24,18,'“You just said his was worse than mine,” said Fred, more irritable than usual.','Restore the explicit comparison.'),
(26,25,'“I’ll try to be anything you want, Mary, if you’ll tell me you love me.”','Restore the direct address to Mary.'),
(31,21,'“Please help me,” she said at last in the same low voice. “Tell me what I can do.”','Restore the scope of her plea.'),
(34,23,'He strained to hold the key out to her as far as he could. Mary drew back again.','Restore distance and repeated retreat.'),
(47,29,'As Rosamond brought Lydgate his tea, he threw down the paper and said to Will, who had jumped up and gone to the table—','Restore the speech lead-in.'),
